---
export const prerender = false;
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Impulse Bot — Juanse Barrio"
  description="Argentina's first chatbot fully dedicated to sexual health. Design and launch of Impulse's conversational channel on WhatsApp."
>

  <div class="page-container">

    <!-- ── HERO ── -->
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">CONVERSATIONAL DESIGN · PUBLIC HEALTH · AI · 2025</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Impulse Bot</h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">Argentina's first chatbot fully dedicated to sexual health.</p>
      <p class="hero-bajada">
        I designed and launched the conversational channel that supported 130+ people during Pride 2025 — from RSVP for the Impulse truck to post-event follow-up.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ── HERO IMAGE ── -->
    <div class="hero-img-wrap">
      <img
        src="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/chatbot_impulse_portada.jpeg"
        alt="Undetectable and Untransmittable — Impulse Bot's two characters embracing on an orange background"
        class="hero-img"
        loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
    </div>

    <!-- ── QUICK FACTS ── -->
    <div class="quick-facts">
      <div class="fact">
        <p class="fact-num">2,249</p>
        <p class="fact-label">Messages exchanged</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <p class="fact-num">196</p>
        <p class="fact-label">Active conversations</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <p class="fact-num">82%</p>
        <p class="fact-label">Opt-in for future communications</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fact">
        <p class="fact-num">#1</p>
        <p class="fact-label">Sexual health chatbot in Argentina</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── META ── -->
    <div class="meta-band">
      <div class="meta-item">
        <p class="mini-eyebrow">Role</p>
        <p class="meta-val">Product Designer & Project Lead</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <p class="mini-eyebrow">Client</p>
        <p class="meta-val">Impulse — AIDS Healthcare Foundation Argentina</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <p class="mini-eyebrow">Timeframe</p>
        <p class="meta-val">Jun 2025 – Apr 2026 (pilot)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <p class="mini-eyebrow">Channel</p>
        <p class="meta-val">WhatsApp Business API</p>
      </div>
      <div class="meta-item">
        <p class="mini-eyebrow">Status</p>
        <p class="meta-val">Pilot closed — evolving to new technology</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── CONTEXT ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">The context</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-title">WhatsApp was where people already were.</h2>
      <div class="prosa">
        <p>
          Impulse is the Argentine chapter of AIDS Healthcare Foundation, the world's leading HIV prevention organization. As part of its Pride 2025 presence, Impulse deployed an <strong>active truck in the march</strong> with testing, information and guest artists. The operation needed a channel that could RSVP and follow up with guests in real time, answer sexual health questions in a warm — non-clinical — tone, and build a contact base that could be reactivated in future campaigns, all with a small team and no call-center budget.
        </p>
        <p>
          Traditional channels (forms, email, social DMs) broke down on at least one of those points. WhatsApp was where people already were.
        </p>
        <p>
          Until this pilot, Argentina had no conversational channel built <em>specifically</em> for sexual health: information lived in static websites, long FAQs, or in-person consultations. A dedicated chatbot opened the door to something different — accurate info, in the user's language, in the user's channel, backed by a trusted organization.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── APPROACH ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">How I built it</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-title">Five decisions that defined the product</h2>

      <div class="decisiones">

        <div class="decision">
          <p class="decision-num">01</p>
          <div>
            <p class="decision-titulo">Conversational mapping before touching the tool</p>
            <p class="decision-cuerpo">
              Before configuring anything, I mapped flows on paper: what are the real questions? What tone do people use when asking about sexual health? What happens when the bot doesn't know? I spent afternoons reading real conversations on other Impulse channels to distill patterns.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <p class="decision-num">02</p>
          <div>
            <p class="decision-titulo">Tone design</p>
            <p class="decision-cuerpo">
              I defined a voice system: close, free of unnecessary jargon, non-judgmental, humorous when appropriate. The hypothesis was that if the user felt judged, they'd leave. The data confirmed it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <p class="decision-num">03</p>
          <div>
            <p class="decision-titulo">Intent-based flows</p>
            <p class="decision-cuerpo">
              Three main branches: (a) RSVP and truck logistics, (b) sexual health info and testing referrals, (c) post-event follow-up. Each branch with a human <em>fallback</em> when the question stepped outside the script.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <p class="decision-num">04</p>
          <div>
            <p class="decision-titulo">WhatsApp as the only channel</p>
            <p class="decision-cuerpo">
              A counterintuitive call — usually you design multichannel. Here, the bet was to concentrate everything on WhatsApp to avoid fragmenting the experience or the support team.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="decision">
          <p class="decision-num">05</p>
          <div>
            <p class="decision-titulo">Metrics from day zero</p>
            <p class="decision-cuerpo">
              Dashboard for received vs. sent messages, active conversations, new contacts, opt-in. Without this, the pilot couldn't justify its evolution.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- Flow chart with lightbox — after all decisions -->
      <div class="flowchart-wrap">
        <button class="flowchart-btn" id="flowchart-trigger" aria-label="View full bot decision tree fullscreen">
          <div class="flowchart-img-area">
            <img
              src="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/dashboard.ong.png"
              alt="Impulse Bot's full decision tree: nodes, branches, global keywords and human fallbacks"
              class="flowchart-img"
              loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="flowchart-hint">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 3h6v6M9 21H3v-6M21 3l-7 7M3 21l7-7"/></svg>
            <span>Expand</span>
          </div>
        </button>
        <p class="flowchart-caption">The bot's full decision tree: three main branches, global keyword handling, and human handoff at every escape point.</p>
      </div>

    </section>

    <!-- Lightbox (outside normal flow) -->
    <div class="lightbox" id="flowchart-lightbox" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Bot decision tree fullscreen">
      <button class="lightbox-close" id="lightbox-close" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
      <div class="lightbox-img-area">
        <img
          src="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/dashboard.ong.png"
          alt="Impulse Bot's full decision tree"
          class="lightbox-img" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── VISUAL SYSTEM ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">Visual system</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-title">Making "Undetectable" and "Untransmittable" human</h2>

      <div class="prosa">
        <p>
          For a sexual health chatbot to work, you first need to dismantle public health language. People don't enter a conversation with the phrase <em>"undetectable viral load"</em> in their heads — they come with doubts, embarrassment, urgency.
        </p>
        <p>
          The bot's visual system was built around <strong>two characters that embody the global U=U slogan (Undetectable = Untransmittable)</strong>: if a person living with HIV has an undetectable viral load thanks to treatment, the virus is sexually untransmittable. It's one of modern prevention's most powerful messages, and it's almost always communicated in medical language.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Undetectable</strong> (blue) came first. <strong>Untransmittable</strong> (red) arrived six months later — the actual time treatment needs to become untransmittable. They're twins. They hug. They jump. They feel scared, they hesitate, they celebrate. They show up in WhatsApp and break the idea that talking about HIV has to be solemn.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="characters-grid">
        <div class="character-card">
          <div class="character-img-area">
            <img
              src="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/chatbot_impulse_pj1.jpeg"
              alt="Undetectable — blue character from Impulse Bot"
              loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="character-info">
            <p class="character-name">Undetectable</p>
            <p class="character-desc">The blue one. Represents an undetectable viral load — the goal of antiretroviral treatment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="character-card">
          <div class="character-img-area">
            <img
              src="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/chatbot_impulse_pj2.jpeg"
              alt="Untransmittable — red character from Impulse Bot"
              loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="character-info">
            <p class="character-name">Untransmittable</p>
            <p class="character-desc">The red one. Arrives six months later — the actual time treatment takes to achieve untransmittability.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="pull-quote">
        "The twins aren't a sticker pack. They're a product decision: if the brand doesn't scare you, the conversation continues."
      </blockquote>

      <a
        href="/images/portfolio/impulse-bot/chatbot_Personajes.pdf"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="pdf-link"
      >
        <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/><polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/></svg>
        Download character manual (PDF)
      </a>
    </section>

    <!-- ── RESULTS ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">Results</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-title">A small pilot that unlocked investment in a new platform.</h2>

      <p class="intro-parrafo">
        Two activation waves — Pride June 2025 and the BA Pride March in October — generated the two spikes of the pilot. Between waves, the bot stayed active and contacts remained in the base, allowing reactivation with no friction.
      </p>

      <!-- ── Native chart ── -->
      <div class="native-chart">
        <div class="chart-top">
          <p class="chart-title">Messages by period · Jun – Oct 2025</p>
          <div class="chart-legend">
            <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot legend-peak"></span>Activation wave</span>
            <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot legend-base"></span>Base activity</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-bars-area">
          <div class="chart-bars">
            <div class="bar-col">
              <span class="bar-val">~900</span>
              <div class="bar-fill bar-peak" style="--h: 100%"></div>
              <div class="bar-foot">
                <span class="bar-month">Jun</span>
                <span class="bar-event">Pride BA</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-col">
              <span class="bar-val"></span>
              <div class="bar-fill bar-base" style="--h: 20%"></div>
              <div class="bar-foot"><span class="bar-month">Jul</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-col">
              <span class="bar-val"></span>
              <div class="bar-fill bar-base" style="--h: 12%"></div>
              <div class="bar-foot"><span class="bar-month">Aug</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-col">
              <span class="bar-val"></span>
              <div class="bar-fill bar-base" style="--h: 14%"></div>
              <div class="bar-foot"><span class="bar-month">Sep</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="bar-col">
              <span class="bar-val">~730</span>
              <div class="bar-fill bar-peak" style="--h: 81%"></div>
              <div class="bar-foot">
                <span class="bar-month">Oct</span>
                <span class="bar-event">BA March</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="chart-ratios">
          <div class="ratio-row">
            <span class="ratio-label">Sent vs. received</span>
            <div class="ratio-track">
              <div class="ratio-fill ratio-a" style="--w: 64.8%">
                <span class="ratio-tick">1,457</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ratio-fill ratio-b" style="--w: 35.2%">
                <span class="ratio-tick">792</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="ratio-row">
            <span class="ratio-label">Opt-in vs. NGO avg (&lt;30%)</span>
            <div class="ratio-track">
              <div class="ratio-fill ratio-a" style="--w: 82%">
                <span class="ratio-tick">82%</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ratio-marker" style="left: 30%">
                <span class="ratio-marker-label">30%</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="metricas-grid">
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">196</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">Active conversations</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">133</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">New contacts</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">2,249</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">Total messages (792 received · 1,457 sent)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">82%</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">Opt-in for future comms (108 of 131 contacts)</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">1.84:1</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">Sent / received message ratio</p>
        </div>
        <div class="metrica">
          <p class="metrica-num">2</p>
          <p class="metrica-label">Activation waves: June Pride + October BA March</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lectura">
        <div class="lectura-item">
          <p class="lectura-titulo">The 1.84:1 ratio is design, not noise</p>
          <p class="lectura-cuerpo">The bot speaks more than it listens because a useful sexual-health conversation includes context, options and referrals — not just binary answers.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lectura-item">
          <p class="lectura-titulo">82% opt-in is exceptionally high for an NGO</p>
          <p class="lectura-cuerpo">Market averages for NGO comms subscriptions usually sit below 30%. It signals the channel built real trust.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="lectura-item">
          <p class="lectura-titulo">The two spikes aren't noise — they're the story</p>
          <p class="lectura-cuerpo">The bot acted as an amplifier in the two key moments of the Argentine LGBTIQ+ calendar. Zero churn between waves: contacts stayed in the base ready to reactivate.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── WHAT I LEARNED ── -->
    <section class="seccion">
      <p class="eyebrow">What I learned</p>
      <h2 class="seccion-title">Four principles the pilot left behind.</h2>

      <div class="aprendizajes">
        <div class="aprendizaje">
          <p class="aprendizaje-titulo">Channel beats sophistication</p>
          <p class="aprendizaje-cuerpo">A rule-based WhatsApp bot beat any "AI-first" solution we could've shipped on another channel. People don't open new apps to talk about sexual health.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aprendizaje">
          <p class="aprendizaje-titulo">Tone is product</p>
          <p class="aprendizaje-cuerpo">Not a cosmetic layer. Every copy decision moved the conversation-continuation metric.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aprendizaje">
          <p class="aprendizaje-titulo">Designing for the human fallback is designing the whole system</p>
          <p class="aprendizaje-cuerpo">Chatbots fail; what matters is how they fail. The human handoff was designed with the same seriousness as the main flow.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="aprendizaje">
          <p class="aprendizaje-titulo">A well-measured pilot is the best case for evolution budget</p>
          <p class="aprendizaje-cuerpo">Without the metrics, this case wouldn't be migrating to a more robust platform today.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── WHAT'S NEXT ── -->
    <section class="seccion seccion-cierre">
      <p class="eyebrow">What's next</p>
      <p class="cierre-texto">
        The pilot closes and the project evolves into a new platform with generative-AI capabilities. The 131 opt-in contacts are the starting point; the tone and flow learnings are the conversational brand playbook.
      </p>
      <p class="videos-eyebrow">Project presentation at Latin American Summit</p>
      <div class="videos-grid">
        <div class="video-wrap">
          <iframe
            src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1191384342?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0"
            frameborder="0"
            allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write"
            allowfullscreen
            loading="lazy"
            title="Latin American Summit presentation — part 1"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
        <div class="video-wrap">
          <iframe
            src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1193265857?title=0&byline=0&portrait=0"
            frameborder="0"
            allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write"
            allowfullscreen
            loading="lazy"
            title="Latin American Summit presentation — part 2"
          ></iframe>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ── CASE NAV ── -->
    <nav class="caso-nav">
      <a href="/en/portfolio" class="caso-nav-link">← View all cases</a>
    </nav>

  </div>

  <script>
    const trigger = document.getElementById('flowchart-trigger');
    const lightbox = document.getElementById('flowchart-lightbox');
    const closeBtn = document.getElementById('lightbox-close');

    trigger?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      lightbox?.classList.add('open');
      document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
    });

    const closeLightbox = () => {
      lightbox?.classList.remove('open');
      document.body.style.overflow = '';
    };

    closeBtn?.addEventListener('click', closeLightbox);
    lightbox?.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      if (e.target === lightbox) closeLightbox();
    });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if (e.key === 'Escape') closeLightbox();
    });
  </script>

</Layout>

<style>
  .page-container {
    max-width: 80rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem);
  }

  .eyebrow {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .mini-eyebrow {
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .hero { padding-top: 8rem; padding-bottom: 3rem; }

  .hero-title {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 0.95;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 1.25rem;
  }

  .hero-subtitle {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 1.75rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: #a0a0a0;
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .hero-bajada {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  }

  .hero-img-wrap {
    width: 100%;
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
    background: #111;
  }

  .hero-img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    max-height: 64vh;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: center center;
  }

  /* ── Quick facts ── */
  .quick-facts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .fact { padding: 2rem; border-right: 1px solid #2a2a2a; background: #141414; }
  .fact:last-child { border-right: none; }

  .fact-num {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .fact-label {
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #6b6b6b;
    margin: 0;
    font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  }

  /* ── Meta ── */
  .meta-band {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
    padding: 2rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2a2a;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .meta-val { font-size: 0.9375rem; color: #c0c0c0; margin: 0; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }

  /* ── Sections ── */
  .seccion { margin-top: 8rem; }

  .seccion-title {
    font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #f0f0f0;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
  }

  .prosa p { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #c0c0c0; max-width: 50rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }
  .prosa p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .prosa strong { color: #f0f0f0; font-weight: 500; }
  .prosa em { color: #e0e0e0; font-style: italic; }

  .intro-parrafo { font-size: 1.125rem; line-height: 1.6; color: #c0c0c0; max-width: 50rem; margin: 0 0 3rem; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }

  /* ── Decisions ── */
  .decisiones { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

  .decision { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr; gap: 3rem; padding: 2.5rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #2a2a2a; }
  .decision:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  .decision-num { font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 3rem; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1; color: #2a2a2a; margin: 0; }
  .decision-titulo { font-family: 'Syne', system-ui, sans-serif; font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 600; color: #f0f0f0; margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
  .decision-cuerpo { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; color: #a0a0a0; margin: 0; max-width: 44rem; font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; }
  .decision-cuerpo em { color: #c0c0c0; font-style: italic; }

  /* ── Flow chart ── */
  .flowchart-wrap { margin: 4rem 0 0; }

  .flowchart-btn {
    position: relative;
    width: 100%;
    background: none;
    border: none;
    padding: 0;
    cursor: zoom-in;
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
